.TH bbcbasic 1 "FUZIX System Utilities" "FUZIX"
.SH NAME
bbcbasic \- BBC BASIC
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bbcbasic
[\fIprogram\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B bbcbasic
is a full BBC BASIC with its own line editor, its own file commands and
an inline assembler.  Started with no argument it comes up at its own
prompt; given a file name it loads that.
.PP
Unlike everything else here it is an interpreter: you type a program in
and run it, with no compile step.  That makes it the quickest way to try
something, and slower than
.BR mmbc (1)
once the program matters.
.SH LOADING A PROGRAM
It reads plain text as well as its own tokenised format, so a program
fetched with
.B fat get
can be loaded directly.
.SH NOTES
Star commands reach the shell.  Where it differs from a real BBC Micro,
and what its graphics and sound words do on this machine, is in the PC3
manual.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mmbc (1),
.BR cc (1),
.BR fforth (1),
.BR fat (1)
